    "updated_at": "2018-04-11T13:50:36Z",
    "body": "Was planning to only check binary using the `binary-data-byte` algorithm, but that only solves the problem for mis-detected ASCII.\r\n\r\nMy main concern are the short signatures - especially the BMP file signature which detects any file starting with the bytes 'BM' as `image/bmp`. Perhaps a better solution is extending the BMP signature - the BMP header has a 2-byte biPlanes member at offset 1A which always contains 0x0001 (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMP_file_format#Example_1)",
